# Ingest fc

Import WireRead from "./wire_read.lg".
Import ProblemRecord from "./problem_record.lg".
Import NodeRecord from "./node_record.lg".
Import RankScore from "./rank_score.lg".
Import RankTrail from "./rank_trail.lg".
Import Rank from "./rank.lg".
Import ManifestEntry from "./manifest_entry.lg".

The formalization lab's whole manifest: every entry a problem, under its
collection, under the lab's cohort. Every entry has a Lean statement and none a
LOGOS one, so each starts `ranked`, waiting for a `formalize` unit, at the atlas's
median prior raised for having a formal statement. A collection ranks as its
best problem, so the graph orders its branches by where the best work is.

## Note
What an ingest produced: problems, and their graph nodes, parents first.

## An Ingested has:
    a problems, which is Seq of Problem.
    a nodes, which is Seq of Node.

## To manifestRank (p: Problem) -> Int:
    Return priority(unprofiledInputs("lean", p's category), noSignals()).

## Note
The problems of a manifest's entries, unique by id.

## To manifestProblems (entries: Seq of Json) -> Result of Seq of Problem and Text:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Problem.
    Let mutable seen be a new Set of Text.
    Repeat for entry in entries:
        Inspect manifestProblem(entry):
            When Err (e):
                Return a new Err with error e.
            When Ok (p):
                If seen contains p's id:
                    Return a new Err with error "the manifest lists {p's id} twice".
                Add p's id to seen.
                Push p to out.
    Return a new Ok with value out.

## Note
The graph of the lab's problems: cohort, collections in first-seen order, problems.

## To manifestNodes (problems: Seq of Problem) -> Seq of Node:
    Let cohort be labCohort().
    Let mutable collections be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable best be a new Map of Text to Int.
    Let mutable top be 0.
    Repeat for p in problems:
        Let home be p's collection.
        If collections contains home is equal to false:
            Push home to collections.
            Set best at home to 0.
        If manifestRank(p) is greater than item home of best:
            Set best at home to manifestRank(p).
        If manifestRank(p) is greater than top:
            Set top to manifestRank(p).
    Let mutable nodes be [rankedNode(cohortNodeId(cohort), none, none, "cohort", "Formalization lab: 200 pinned open statements", top)].
    Repeat for c in collections:
        Push rankedNode(collectionNodeId(cohort, c), some cohortNodeId(cohort), none, "collection", c, item c of best) to nodes.
    Repeat for p in problems:
        Push rankedNode(problemNodeId(p's id), some collectionNodeId(cohort, p's collection), some p's id, "problem", p's title, manifestRank(p)) to nodes.
    Return nodes.

## Note
A manifest document, ingested.

## To ingestManifest (text: Text) -> Result of Ingested and Text:
    Inspect parseStrict(text):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "the manifest is not JSON: " + e.
        When Ok (doc):
            Inspect jsonGet(doc, "problems"):
                When JArr (entries):
                    Inspect manifestProblems(entries):
                        When Err (e):
                            Return a new Err with error e.
                        When Ok (problems):
                            Return a new Ok with value (a new Ingested with problems problems and nodes manifestNodes(problems)).
                Otherwise:
                    Return a new Err with error "the manifest has no problems array".
    Return a new Err with error "unreadable manifest".
